        "title": "10 - The Type Industry: Foundries, Licensing, and the Business of Type",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The type industry is one of the oldest continuously operating software businesses — fonts are intellectual property sold under license. The structural parallels to the software industry are direct: companies sell intangible products, manage IP portfolios through acquisition, deal with piracy, and have gone through the full arc from craft monopolies to commoditization via open source."
